<aside class="kh-note-box">
<span class="kh-note-box__label">What's a colophon?</span>
Historically a colophon summarized how a book was made — who printed it, where, and when. On the web, a colophon is a short page describing how a site is built and the principles behind it (see <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colophon_(publishing)">colophon in publishing</a> and <a href="https://indieweb.org/colophon">IndieWeb colophon</a>).
</span>
</aside>

{% markdown %}

This site is built and published with a small, readable stack and a bias for flexibility and performance.

## Stack

- **Static site generator**: [Eleventy (11ty) v3](https://www.11ty.dev/)
- **Language & tooling**: Node.js (Yarn scripts), Nunjucks templates, Markdown via Markdown‑It with `markdown-it-anchor`
- **Styles**: Sass compiled to a single CSS file; custom utility classes; normalize; type set with the Recursive font
  - Previously used the EMBL Visual Framework (VF) and Gulp; the [migration to a simpler Eleventy v3 stack is documented here](/posts/20250831-site-overhaul-eleventy-v3).
- **Search**: Static index generated at build time; client‑side search with Lunr.js. Source: [search page template](https://github.com/khawkins98/allaboutken-11ty/blob/main/src/site/search.njk), [client‑side script](https://github.com/khawkins98/allaboutken-11ty/blob/main/src/site/js-search-client-side.js), [index builder](https://github.com/khawkins98/allaboutken-11ty/blob/main/scripts/build-search-index.js)
- **Hosting**: Vercel (auto‑deploys from GitHub, automatic HTTPS, CDN)
- **Domain**: Cloudflare (DNS, security, performance)
- Fonts: [Recursive](/posts/20250904-switching-to-recursive)

## Build & source

- **Source code**: [`github.com/khawkins98/allaboutken-11ty`](https://github.com/khawkins98/allaboutken-11ty/)
- **Images**: [Eleventy Image plugin](https://www.11ty.dev/docs/plugins/image) ([Sharp](https://sharp.pixelplumbing.com/) under the hood) configured to [generate deterministic, token‑based filenames](/posts/20250907-deterministic-image-filenames)
- **Build command**: `yarn build` → compiles Sass, runs Eleventy, processes images, builds search index

## Privacy

- **Analytics**: [GoatCounter](https://www.goatcounter.com/) (cookie‑free, aggregate counts only). See their rationale on GDPR consent and legitimate interest: [GDPR consent notices](https://khawkins98.goatcounter.com/help/gdpr).
- **No trackers**: No ad tech, no cross‑site profiling.

## Principles

- Prefer simple, inspectable pages over heavy frameworks.
- Ship as little JS as practical; keep content readable without it.
- Optimize images and typography for legibility.
- Document decisions in public when it helps future me (and you).

